UID:7772@2026@be.digitalia.fosdem
DTSTAMP:20260201T185751Z
DTSTART:20260201T160000Z
DTEND:20260201T165000Z
SUMMARY:Open Source Security in spite of AI
DESCRIPTION:The curl project has been bombarded by large volumes of low quality AI slop security reports and Daniel shows examples. Sloppy humans causing Denial-of-Service attacks by overloading maintainers with quickly produced almost-real-looking rubbish.
 At the same time, upcoming new AI powered tools find flaws and mistakes in existing code in ways no previous code analyzers have been able to. Daniel names names and shows examples of findings, some that even feels almost human. Next level bug-hunting for sure.
 AI now simultaneously brings us the worst and the best.
X-ALT-DESC:<p>The curl project has been bombarded by large volumes of low quality AI slop security reports and Daniel shows examples. Sloppy humans causing Denial-of-Service attacks by overloading maintainers with quickly produced almost-real-looking rubbish.</p>
 <p>At the same time, upcoming new AI powered tools find flaws and mistakes in existing code in ways no previous code analyzers have been able to. Daniel names names and shows examples of findings, some that even feels almost human. Next level bug-hunting for sure.</p>
 <p>AI now simultaneously brings us the worst and the best.</p>
